# Line endings: LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# This repository is built and audited on Linux (WSL) and its shell scripts must
# run there, so LF is the only line ending that is always correct. `eol=lf`
# states that explicitly for text files instead of leaving it to each machine's
# core.autocrlf - which is what caused the trouble:
#
#   * core.autocrlf=true was set to stop WSL git reporting every text file as
#     modified, because the trees had been checked out on Windows with CRLF.
#   * A rebase then rewrote the shell scripts through that setting, and bash
#     refused them: "scripts/wsl-build.sh: line 8: set: pipefail: invalid
#     option name". The build died before doing any work.
#   * Setting it to false brought the phantom modifications back, and
#     renormalizing then made all 40 tracked files look modified at once.
#
# The two settings cannot both be right, and neither is the right tool: they
# apply one blanket rule to files that need opposite ones. This file is.
# It travels with the repository, so it holds whatever a contributor's own
# core.autocrlf happens to say.
#
# The whole tree is committed with LF. Windows checkouts also get LF, which is
# correct for Gradle, Kotlin, Go and XML, and the only workable choice for the
# scripts in scripts/.

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Interpreted by a POSIX shell. Named explicitly because `text=auto` only
# applies the rule to files it detects as text, and a script with CRLF is not
# merely misformatted - it will not execute.
*.sh            text eol=lf
gradlew         text eol=lf

# Windows launchers, kept CRLF because cmd.exe requires it.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Never touched: these are not text, and a line-ending filter would corrupt
# them silently rather than loudly.
*.apk           binary
*.aar           binary
*.jar           binary
*.jks           binary
*.keystore      binary
*.so            binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.webp          binary
*.ico           binary
